{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_9100852f391448b870958843003f22766864e572d3db56cd5de135dcfca16bc2", "title": "Lucknow", "text": "Lucknow( Lakhna'ū ) is the capital of the Indian state of Uttar Pradesh and is also the administrative headquarters of the eponymous District and Division.", "score": 28.6771}, {"id": "hp_doc_3a61789979774b1d4c47a394a4c8cf52f360f45ad5e5f6c87d899d7373ece351", "title": "Hakim Syed Khaleefathullah", "text": "Syed Khaleefathullah was born in 1938, in Chennai, the capital city of the south Indian state of Tamil Nadu. He studied Unani in the traditional way, and started his medical practice in Chennai. In 1985, he founded Niamath Science Academy, an NGO in memory of the renowned Unani physician, Dr. Hakim Syed Niamathullah, for promoting the Unani medicine system.", "score": 12.9618}, {"id": "hp_doc_7b2b748c8cb11e977b4ee6ed9abb0dc57881a750893329140f2d05e38f8f2812", "title": "Ahmed and Mohammed Hussain", "text": "Ahmed Hussain and Mohammed Hussain are ghazal singers from Jaipur, capital of Rajasthan state in India. Ahmed and Mohammed Hussain are two brothers who sing classical ghazals. Born in Rajasthan as sons of the famous ghazal and thumri singer Ustad Afzal Hussain, the duo touches genres like Indian classical music and bhajan as well as ghazal. They started their singing career in 1958 as classical and thumri artists. Their first album \"Guldasta\" was released in 1980 and was successful. Since then they have released about 50 albums. They attempted popularizing their music by turning to tempo music in Maan bhi ja.", "score": 10.438}], "remaining_searches": 1}
